From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] powrprof, user32: power schemes, the platform role, power notifications

Chrome, Electron programs and games ask for the power plan's display and
sleep timeouts and the platform role; the calls failed or lied:

- Power schemes (new dlls/powrprof/schemes.c): the three every system has
  (Balanced, High performance, Power saver) with their subgroups (display,
  hard disk, sleep, buttons and lid, processor, battery) and settings and
  each setting's default AC and DC index; what is changed, the active
  scheme and schemes of one's own under
  HKLM\System\CurrentControlSet\Control\Power\User\PowerSchemes.
  - PowerGetActiveScheme, PowerReadACValue/PowerReadDCValue,
    PowerEnumerate and PowerReadFriendlyName returned
    ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED; PowerSetActiveScheme and
    PowerWriteACValueIndex returned success and kept nothing.
  - New: PowerRead/WriteAC/DCValueIndex, PowerReadAC/DCDefaultIndex,
    PowerReadDescription, PowerWriteFriendlyName/Description,
    PowerDuplicateScheme, PowerDeleteScheme (not the active one),
    PowerRestoreDefaultPowerSchemes, PowerRestoreIndividualDefaultPowerScheme,
    PowerCanRestoreIndividualDefaultPowerScheme, PowerReadValueMin/Max/
    Increment/UnitsSpecifier, PowerReadPossibleValue/FriendlyName,
    PowerReadSettingAttributes, PowerSettingAccessCheck(Ex).
- PowerDeterminePlatformRole(Ex) always said "desktop": the role is from the
  SMBIOS system enclosure's chassis type (desktop, mobile, slate, server,
  appliance), a chassis that does not say with a battery being mobile; a
  slate is mobile to version 1 callers, an unknown version unspecified.
- PowerSettingRegisterNotification gave 0xdeadbeef and never called back:
  as on Windows the current value is sent at once (the active scheme, its
  personality, the scheme's settings, the power source, battery, display,
  lid, presence) and again when this process changes it.
  PowerRegisterSuspendResumeNotification keeps real registrations (Wine has
  no source of suspend and resume events to send them).
- user32: RegisterPowerSettingNotification's first value of the active
  scheme and personality is the scheme powrprof keeps active (it was always
  Balanced).

Gate: test/powerschemes-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, test/powerschemes-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_ACTIVE_NOT_KEPT, SG_MUTANT_NO_INITIAL_VALUE,
SG_MUTANT_ROLE_ANY_VERSION (powrprof/schemes.c).
---
